---
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
import Scene from "../components/Scene.astro";
import RequestJourney from "../components/RequestJourney.astro";
import { url, github } from "../lib/site";
const packages = [
  {
    id: "Wafish.Runtime",
    role: "01 / GATEWAY",
    detail: "The YARP request pipeline and built-in policy plugins.",
  },
  {
    id: "Wafish.Storage.Sqlite",
    role: "02 / STORAGE",
    detail:
      "Persist gateway configuration in SQLite, with optional encryption.",
  },
  {
    id: "Wafish.Administration",
    role: "03 / MANAGEMENT · OPTIONAL",
    detail: "Authenticated APIs for configuration and gateway operations.",
  },
  {
    id: "Wafish.ReactUi",
    role: "04 / DASHBOARD · OPTIONAL",
    detail: "A web workspace for routes, policies, logs, and traffic.",
  },
  {
    id: "Wafish.Client",
    role: "05 / SERVICE REGISTRATION · OPTIONAL",
    detail: "Let your ASP.NET Core services register with the gateway.",
  },
];
---

<Shell>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN-SOURCE REVERSE PROXY + REQUEST
        POLICIES
      </p>
      <h1>
        An API gateway.
        <br />
        <span>Built for .NET.</span>
      </h1>
      <div class="hero-bottom">
        <p>
          Wafish routes HTTP traffic to your services using YARP. Add a web
          application firewall, rate limits, caching, and retries. Change routes
          and policies live through APIs or an optional web dashboard.
        </p>
        <a class="button signal" href={url("docs/getting-started/")}>
          Build your gateway <span>↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-instrument">
      <RequestJourney />
      <div class="instrument-index">
        <span>FIG. 001 / FOLLOW THE REQUEST</span>
        <span>ONE REQUEST. EACH DECISION. THE NEXT STEP.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="release-strip mono">
      <span>01 / OPEN SOURCE · MIT</span>
      <span>02 / .NET 10 + YARP 2.3</span>
      <a href={url("docs/release-notes/")}>
        03 / 1.0.0-rc.1 · RELEASE CANDIDATE ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="capabilities wrap">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / THE OPERATING LAYER</p>
      <h2>
        Less glue.
        <br />
        More gateway.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Keep YARP’s forwarding engine. Add the tools that make a gateway yours.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-list">
      <a href={url("docs/configuration/")}>
        <span class="item-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Change it while it runs.</h3>
          <p>
            Preview configuration. Apply versioned changes. Inspect what
            persisted and what became active.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="item-arrow">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href={url("docs/plugins/")}>
        <span class="item-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Policy, with a place to live.</h3>
          <p>
            12 built-in plugins. Scoped bindings. WAF, rate limits, cache,
            retry, and circuit-breaking controls.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="item-arrow">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href={url("docs/operations/")}>
        <span class="item-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Know what is happening.</h3>
          <p>
            Request logs, latency distributions, audit records, and destination
            health. One connected view.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="item-arrow">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href={url("docs/registration/")}>
        <span class="item-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Let services come to you.</h3>
          <p>
            Client registration, renewable leases, graceful draining, and
            discovery from external registries.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="item-arrow">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="console-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="console-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / A WORKSPACE FOR OPERATORS</p>
          <h2>
            See the system.
            <br />
            Make the change.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Routes, clusters, policies, and their history.
          <br />A React administration workspace you can include
          <br class="desktop" /> when your deployment needs it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="console-figure">
        <div class="window-bar mono">
          <span>
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
          </span>
          <span>WAFISH / ADMINISTRATION</span>
          <span>DEMO FIXTURE</span>
        </div>
        <img
          src={url("images/console-routes.webp")}
          alt="Wafish administration workspace showing configured routes, destinations, and route controls in an isolated demo."
          width="1440"
          height="960"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Real interface. Isolated demonstration data.{" "}
          <a href={url("docs/administration/")}>Explore the workspace ↗</a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="console-details">
        <div>
          <span class="mono">INSPECT</span>
          <p>Trace a decision through logs and audit history.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">CONFIGURE</span>
          <p>Use forms or work directly with the YARP schema.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">CONTROL</span>
          <p>Keep read and write permissions explicit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="under-hood wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 / ENGINEERING YOU CAN EXPLAIN</p>
    <div class="section-row">
      <h2>Not a black box.</h2>
      <p>
        Step through a public cache fill.
        <br />
        See exactly when the upstream does work.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Scene kind="cache" compact />
    <div class="under-caption">
      <p>
        Illustrated behavior, not a performance benchmark. Cache sharing is
        local to each process.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={url("presentation/")}>
        See all six demonstrations <span>↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="composition wrap">
    <div class="composition-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / INSTALL THE PACKAGES YOU NEED</p>
      <h2>
        Start small.
        <br />
        Add what you need.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Run the proxy on its own. Add administration, the UI, or client
        registration as your system grows.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={url("docs/architecture/")}>
        Read the architecture ↗
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="package-installation">
      <ol class="package-list" aria-label="Install Wafish packages">
        {packages.map(({ id, role, detail }) => (
          <li>
            <div class="package-meta">
              <span>{role}</span>
              <a
                href={`https://www.nuget.org/packages/${id}`}
                aria-label={`${id} on NuGet.org`}
              >
                NuGet.org <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </div>
            <code class="package-command">
              dotnet add package <strong>{id}</strong>
              <span class="package-version"> --version 1.0.0-rc.1</span>
            </code>
            <p>{detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="package-note">
        First release candidate. These commands require publication to
        NuGet.org. Use the{" "}
        <a href={url("docs/getting-started/")}>source checkout guide</a> until
        then.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="talk-invite wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">05 / TAKE IT TO THE ROOM</span>
    <div>
      <h2>
        A gateway.
        <br />
        In motion.
      </h2>
      <p>
        A 27-minute technical talk. Six interactive models.
        <br />
        Speaker notes, an offline edition, and a PDF handout.
      </p>
      <a class="button signal" href={url("presentation/")}>
        Open the presentation <span>↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="talk-number" aria-hidden="true">
      27<span>MINUTES</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="start-section wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT REQUEST STARTS HERE</p>
    <h2>Make it your gateway.</h2>
    <p>Linux, Windows, and macOS. .NET 10. Open source.</p>
    <div class="start-actions">
      <a class="button signal" href={url("docs/getting-started/")}>
        Get started <span>↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="button outline" href={github}>
        Explore the source <span>↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="release-note">
      First release candidate. Package publication is pending.{" "}
      <a href={url("docs/release-notes/")}>Read the support boundaries.</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Shell>
